  "description": "SQLite provider for Unified.Data.Tables: IStorage<T> and IPolymorphicStorage<TBase> over one local database file (or :memory:), for development, single-machine deployments and durable tests. The same engine as the in-memory provider, so rows round-trip through the real TableEntitySerializer and the Table service's rules hold (key rules, 100 rows and the payload budget a transaction, 64 KiB a cell, 1 MB a row): a table that works here works on Azure Table Storage. Write-ahead logging with one writer and many readers, several processes on one machine, ETags from a database-wide counter, large values in the same split layout with offloaded blobs in the database, provider-neutral failures, and every 0.10.0 side interface (conditional delete, atomic batches, storage info, raw tables). No Azure provider package, no Azure.Storage.Blobs, no network.",
